sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Ingress as Platform Ingress<br/>Route / Gateway (outside repo)<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant API as vllm-cpu API server<br/>uvicorn 8000/TCP HTTP
    participant Engine as Engine core process<br/>(in-pod)
    participant Store as HF Hub / S3 / ModelScope<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Prom as Prometheus<br/>(user workload monitoring)

    Note over API,Store: Flow 2: Model load at startup
    API->>Store: Download weights / tokenizer<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS (system OpenSSL)<br/>HF_TOKEN / S3 keys / MODELSCOPE_API_TOKEN / none
    Store-->>API: Model artifacts (or local PVC)
    API->>Engine: Start engine core, load model on CPU

    Note over Client,Engine: Flow 1: Inference request via KServe ServingRuntime
    Client->>Ingress: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>HTTPS/443 TLS, platform-defined auth
    Ingress->>API: HTTP/8000 (HTTPS if --ssl-* set)<br/>Authorization: Bearer API key (opt-in)
    API->>Engine: Request via ZeroMQ local IPC<br/>no encryption, no auth (in-pod)
    Engine-->>API: Generated tokens
    API-->>Ingress: JSON / SSE stream
    Ingress-->>Client: HTTPS response

    Note over Client,API: Root-level routes are never guarded by vLLM
    Client->>Ingress: POST /tokenize, /score, /scale_elastic_ep ...
    Ingress->>API: HTTP/8000, no vLLM auth

    Note over Prom,API: Flow 3: Metrics scrape
    Prom->>API: GET /metrics<br/>HTTP/8000, no encryption, no auth
    API-->>Prom: Prometheus exposition
